# EventHub booking-management coverage

| ID | Coverage |
|---|---|
| BKG-01 | Single-ticket booking, confirmation, reference format, saved booking details |
| BKG-02 | Multiple-ticket quantity and calculated total |
| BKG-03 | Quantity lower and upper boundaries |
| BKG-04 | Invalid customer name, email, and phone |
| BKG-05 | Sold-out event |
| BKG-06 | Over-capacity rejection and exact remaining capacity |
| BKG-07 | Booking details in My Bookings |
| BKG-08 | Booking visibility isolation between accounts |
| BKG-09 | Dismissing a cancellation |
| BKG-10 | Confirming cancellation |
| BKG-11 | Repeated cancellation safety |
| BKG-12 | Authentication required for My Bookings |
| BKG-13 | Zero-price event |
| BKG-14 | Event inventory consumed before confirmation |
| BKG-15 | Configured per-user booking limit |

Cancellation behavior is asserted only where documented by the API (`cancelled` status); the suite does not assert seat restoration. BKG-15 requires the actual sandbox limit and a fresh account.
